# Either of two optional fields may be added first, and the order of the keys follows that. The store loads the slot and compares it with the bit pattern of an empty slot.
# A slot that is filled, the likely case, is stored into at once. Only the store that adds the field goes on to record the order, on an unlikely path.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="widen" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[width]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[isNumber]] = Equal(b@[[width]], b@[[width]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNumber]], Terminal,
# CHECK: Double b@[[stored]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[style]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[old]] = Load(b@[[style]], offset = [[slot]], ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlotOrAdd)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isEmpty]] = Equal(b@[[old]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isEmpty]], Terminal,
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:Unlikely:#[[add]], Else:#[[store]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[store]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors:
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[stored]], b@[[style]], offset = [[slot]], ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:PutSlotOrAdd)
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[add]]:
# CHECK: Load(b@[[style]], offset = 8, ControlDependent|Reads:OrderWords
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The count takes in the moves around the call on the unlikely path, which follow the calling convention.
# X64-LABEL: name="widen" role=Source
# X64-NEXT: instructions: 18, patchpoints: 1
# ARM64-LABEL: name="widen" role=Source
# ARM64-NEXT: instructions: 22, patchpoints: 1
